# Format on type

Nothing here needs a command. The language server reacts to the keys you type.

## Tables realign on the closing pipe

[inventory] := table
| item   | count | price |
| ------ | ----- | ----- |
| pencil | 40    | $0.50 |
| eraser | 12    | $1.25 |

<!-- Add a row below the last one: type | strawberry | 3 | $4.00 |
When you type the final |, every row realigns. The row you are typing is only
padded once every column has a cell, and only its spaces change. -->

[stock_value] := sum(inventory, count * price)
Stock value: [stock_value].

## Checklists continue on Enter

- [ ] Put the cursor at the end of this line and press Enter
- [ ] A new empty checkbox appears with the same indent
  - [ ] Nested items keep their indentation
- [ ] Press Enter twice on an empty checkbox to end the list

Plain paragraphs are never turned into tasks.
